{"session_id":"golden-session-01","asked":["q1","q2"],"last_turn":{"turn_order":1,"transcript":"For a high traffic API serving millions of requests per day I would design a two tier caching layer with Redis for hot keys and CDN edge cache for static responses. The cache invalidation strategy would use time to live of sixty seconds for volatile data and explicit purge on write for critical entities. I would handle cache stampede with request coalescing and a background refresh using a lock with five second timeout so only one worker rebuilds the entry. This approach reduced p95 latency from three hundred milliseconds to forty milliseconds in my previous role at FintechCorp while we shipped the new checkout flow for fifty thousand daily users. I also added observability with hit ratio metrics and alerts when the ratio drops below eighty percent to ensure reliability.","formatted":true,"end_of_turn":true,"end_of_turn_confidence":0.92,"words":[{"text":"For","start":125000,"end":125250,"confidence":0.92,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"a","start":125350,"end":125600,"confidence":0.9400000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"high","start":125700,"end":125950,"confidence":0.9600000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"traffic","start":126050,"end":126300,"confidence":0.92,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"API","start":126400,"end":126650,"confidence":0.9400000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"serving","start":126750,"end":127000,"confidence":0.9600000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"millions","start":127100,"end":127350,"confidence":0.92,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"of","start":127450,"end":127700,"confidence":0.9400000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"requests","start":127800,"end":128050,"confidence":0.9600000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"per","start":128150,"end":128400,"confidence":0.92,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"day","start":128500,"end":128750,"confidence":0.9400000000000001,"word_is_final":false},{"text":"I","start"